SALMONpy third-party notices

The bundled SALMON-derived kernels use the repository's Apache-2.0 license.
Platform wheels can include OpenBLAS and GCC/Fortran runtimes; their notices are
preserved in packaging/ld/licenses/ and installed as salmonpy/licenses/:

- OpenBLAS-LICENSE.txt
- GCC-RUNTIME-EXCEPTION.txt
- GPL-3.0.txt
- LGPL-2.1.txt
- NOTICE.txt

macOS kernel wheels link the operating system Accelerate framework.
Python dependencies (NumPy and optional ASE/f90nml/Matplotlib) retain their own
installed licenses; they are dependencies, not copied Python source here.

The optional external full SALMON runtime has its own LICENSE.THIRD-PARTY and
ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS, obtained from the pinned upstream source. Its FFTE, bundled
linear algebra, Libxc and other application-specific notices are not replaced
by this package notice. No FFTE, full LAPACK or full SALMON application sources
are bundled in SALMONpy's native/ directory.

The Si introductory example includes the unmodified Si_rps.dat distributed at
samples/exercise_04_bulkSi_gs/Si_rps.dat in SALMON2 commit
3322d0561c0cad5180679136b3eddbe8b909487c. Its upstream Apache-2.0 LICENSE and
source/hash provenance are retained in salmonpy/examples/si_intro_data/.
This legacy KY data file does not encode pseudopotential-generator metadata;
the starter follows its accompanying upstream PZ example and does not certify
transferability or convergence for other conditions.

Bundled full solver snapshots: see runtime/sources/standard/LICENSE.THIRD-PARTY
and runtime/sources/hse-fast-reference/LICENSE.THIRD-PARTY, including their
ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS and file-specific license headers. These notices are retained
in installed source resources and in explicitly packaged solver runtimes.

Optical numerical reference data
-------------------------------
The curated numerical subset in salmonpy/optical_data/raw is from the
refractiveindex.info-database, distributed under CC0 1.0 Universal by its
maintainer. Its unmodified CC0 text is salmonpy/optical_data/CC0-1.0.txt.
Pinned source commit, original file paths/URLs, SHA256 and original experimental
citations are in salmonpy/optical_data/catalog.json. Derived passive LD candidates
are labeled separately from the original measurements. Original journal articles,
figures and website content are not included. This data dedication does not
change the license of SALMONpy code or the original publications.
Database citation: M. N. Polyanskiy, Scientific Data 11, 94 (2024),
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02898-2.
